{"id": "EUVD-2026-103780", "enisaUuid": "315c9c59-ec37-3201-8469-befd29b8549c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvc_screen: reload vc pointer before if (ret) in vcs_write() to avoid UAF\n\nThe reload of 'vc' added by commit 8fb9ea65c9d1 (\"vc_screen: reload load\nof struct vc_data pointer in vcs_write() to avoid UAF\") sits after the\n'if (ret)' block, so the copy-failure break path exits the loop without\nreloading vc. If the vc was kfree()'d via vc_port_destruct during the\nunlocked copy_from_user() window, the post-loop\n'if (written && vc) vcs_scr_updated(vc)' is reached with a stale\nnon-NULL vc. The '&& vc' guard from commit a287620312dc (\"vc_screen:\nfix null-ptr-deref in vcs_notifier() during concurrent vcs_write\") only\nhandles the NULL case, not this stale-non-NULL case; vcs_notifier() then\nreads param->vc->vc_num from freed memory:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in vcs_notifier+0x7c/0xd0\n  Read of size 2 at addr ffff888007149190\n  Call Trace:\n   vcs_notifier+0x7c/0xd0\n   atomic_notifier_call_chain+0x70/0xa0\n   vcs_scr_updated+0x77/0xa0\n   vcs_write+0x71b/0x7e0\n  Allocated by task: vc_allocate -> con_install -> tty_open\n  Freed by task: kfree <- vt_ioctl (VT_DISALLOCATE -> vc_port_destruct)\n\nMove the reload to immediately after console_lock(), before 'if (ret)',\nso every break path below passes a fresh vc to the post-loop\nvcs_scr_updated().", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:50:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:25", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c073d01f6f5367c3a4f07efd507274ed0d03acd0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1485a3dd97ab1af2605243cabe6b604546d46dd1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/233a2e190b12884d186027d0b86d43a48799b69c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9dfcadc5e003fb250dd471db90144bd5366140e9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/226bd5603371cd9f6642cbb9e9a677f445de3530"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98840", "GHSA-vpw3-5qwq-wxvw"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "012ea239-0cb0-3445-902e-b262b1028a68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "077a625b-e1b5-35d6-8890-202221890105", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "0a57060b-0492-3caf-bb4d-1819e88bb5ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "0b21f5fb-0881-3993-8cde-4da469bc9623", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.211 <5.16"}, {"id": "11018a5a-d51f-381b-836a-a9de57240b47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7cc3dd79777f6ae4625ec37e84dd18a26dc88bde <233a2e190b12884d186027d0b86d43a48799b69c"}, {"id": "288834c3-8f6b-37c9-b0e2-af3c561248ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0.14 <7.1"}, {"id": "2a05c657-28f9-3e61-bf83-ae0a73cf8d85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3b3cef4e-9cd2-357c-b7bd-4f916f4430e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.144 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "3e24b1e3-8cb9-35c1-8f56-61fecbece27d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.95 <6.12.113"}, {"id": "47c33914-767a-378c-a566-1571524d1840", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ff4806202749a51938236214adc0281481a57366"}, {"id": "4d49a105-9e35-300c-98e0-61a5030c411a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "43a6281790273c1b0a9ab76609ff0245b968f1e6"}, {"id": "5e6cc9d5-97f6-3ab0-8096-8e481d7756c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.37 <6.18.56"}, {"id": "6ae456f0-241e-3237-bb3b-17fd86f424aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}